Concept: Player selection of character skills will interact meaningfully with the enemy, e.g. depleting its hit points, ending the encounter once equal to 0. If this fails and there is no foreseeable solution, the focus of development will pivot to the visual novel concept.

This requires functional interaction between the UI and outlined behaviors of the characters. If the UI breaks in some way, or if the character skills do not behave properly, the core gameplay loop cannot work.

The player should be able to damage the enemy with the characters' attack skills, and if the enemy's hit points reach 0, the game should switch to a win screen.
